1. Log in to the Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform web console
    $oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
    $oc whoami --show-console


2. View the cluster version on the Overview page for the cluster.
    From the Home → Overview page, scroll down to view the cluster details.
    Locate the OpenShift version in the Details section.
    - see the nodes cluster
    - go to the Master Terminal and check the kubelet service
    - see The cluster Utilization
    - see the main projects (api-server, etcd, controller ....)


3. Open the terminal
    oc get clusterversion
    oc get nodes
    oc get co


